# Keeps the dev-iteration build context small when a host checkout is passed in
# via `--build-context vision_src=$HOME/dev/vision.cpp`. Without this the COPY
# drags ~3.2 GB of local build trees and downloaded GGUFs into the builder.
#
# The Dockerfile also purges build dirs after the COPY — that is the load-bearing
# guard (a stale CMakeCache.txt names the host's source path and makes cmake
# refuse to configure). This file is the speed half of the same problem.
build/
build-*/
models/
.git/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.o
*.so
